<p>Nestlé said thieves stole a truck carrying 413,793 KitKat bars from its new chocolate range during transit in Europe last week. The shipment weighed about 12 tonnes and was traveling from central Italy toward Poland. The company said the vehicle and its cargo are still missing, and that it is working with local authorities and supply chain partners as the investigation continues. The loss matters because the shipment was meant for distribution in multiple countries along the route. KitKat warned that some stores could run short ahead of Easter.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/OxliaQsV1HKaDh6CBK4_JAxbi74dmqOb4fbBG_ABpkrOlLGwUKcENxHDiT22lMLFtVgXK09zh2BtcD1z9FhA-QScmx0Y9m23Z4lvshVcR6eD' alt='A pack of KitKat bars displayed at Nestlé’s showroom in Vevey in a 2016 file photo.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Product labeling: Nestlé described the cargo as part of a &quot;new chocolate range,&quot; while The Guardian identified the bars as the brand’s new F1 line.</li><li>Disclosure gap: KitKat said the truck left central Italy for Poland, but did not say where along that route it disappeared.</li><li>Timing marker: AFP, cited by The Guardian, said thieves pilfered the truck on 26 March while it was driving through Europe.</li></ul><blockquote>We’ve always encouraged people to have a break with KitKat, but it seems thieves have taken the message too literally and made a break with more than 12 tonnes of our chocolate. - KitKat spokesperson</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Media coverage focused on both the scale of the theft and KitKat’s &quot;have a break&quot; slogan, casting it as an unusually theatrical chocolate heist rather than routine retail theft. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/nestle-says-thieves-stole-12-tons-of-kitkat-chocolate-bars/a-76579815'>DW</a>, <a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/28/kitkat-stolen-italy-f1-bar'>The Guardian</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/nestle-says-thieves-stole-12-tons-of-kitkat-chocolate-bars/a-76579815'>Nestle says thieves stole 12 tons of KitKat chocolate bars</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/over-4-lakh-kitkat-bars-stolen-after-leaving-factory-in-italy-for-poland-11280304#publisher=newsstand'>Over 4,00,000 Kitkat Bars Stolen From Cargo Enroute Poland From Italy</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1986312/sweet-heist-nestle-says-12-tonnes-of-kitkat-stolen-in-europe'>Sweet heist? Nestle says 12 tonnes of KitKat stolen in Europe</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/28/kitkat-stolen-italy-f1-bar'>Sugar high(st): more than twelve tons of KitKat’s ‘new chocolate range’ stolen in Italy</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3348270/over-400000-kitkat-bars-stolen-thieves-make-break-12-tonne-shipment'>Over 400,000 KitKat bars stolen, as thieves ‘make a break’ with 12 tonne shipment</a> - scmp.com</li></ul>